B  flatness and conformal invariance
  [OK] B1  g ~ 1/r (flat curve) from the deep kernel mu ~ x^s requires s = d - 2
  [OK] B2  inversion x -> x/|x|^2 maps int |grad Phi|^p d^dx to itself iff 2p - d - 1 = d - 1, i.e. p = d  (s = d - 2)
  [OK] B3  chain rule: dPhi~/dr' = -(1/r'^2) Phi'(r) with r = 1/r' (so |grad Phi| = r'^2 |grad Phi~|)
  [OK] B4  the fixed kernel s=1 (p=3) is conformally invariant iff d = 3 (2p-d-1 = d-1 -> d = 3)
  [OK] B5  control: s = 1 at d = 4 gives exponent 2p-d-1 = 1 != d-1 = 3 (not invariant); s = d-2 = 2 at d = 4 gives p = 4 = d (invariant)

